  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 45 actions (actions.js, returned by getActionDefinitions) and no feedbacks (the module never calls setFeedbackDefinitions). Two further actions (selectClipForPreview, takeClipById) are commented out in the source (actions.js:327-353, \"Need clarification on the ID expected here\") and are not catalogued.",
    "Protocol: plain text commands of two characters (plus a clip number for the two clip actions) sent without terminator over TCP port 4647 (default) or UDP port 7000, chosen by the config dropdown prot (ids tcp and udp, default tcp); host has Regex.IP and no default (config.js, main.js:57-110). Nothing is read back, so there is no state, variables or feedback.",
    "Each action description lists the command text it sends (self.send). Several actions send the same command: play and resumePgm both send PL.",
    "The two clip actions define their number option without default, min, max or step (the source only sets type, label and id), and use different label capitalisation (loadClip \"clip ID\", loadAndTakeClip \"Clip ID\"). The callbacks apply parseInt(value, 10) and send it directly after GO or GT. Valid clip ids are not defined in the module.",
    "The actions marked \"has no effect??\" in the source (pgmGotoIn, pgmGotoOut, pvwGotoIn, pvwGotoOut) are recorded as written; whether the device ignores these commands was not checked.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.4.0: options do not support expressions."
  ],
